.TH TULPAR-GRAPH 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.4.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-graph \- export the installed package dependency graph
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar graph
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ package ]
.br
.B tulpar p
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ package ]
.br
.B tulpar \-p
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ package ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Builds libapg's dependency graph from installed packages and
exports it in Graphviz DOT format. When an optional
.I package
name is supplied, only the transitive dependency subgraph rooted at that
package is exported. Every package is a node (installed
ones filled green), every dependency is an edge to whatever provider
libapg would currently resolve it to (labeled with the version
constraint, if any; drawn red and dashed if unresolved), and every
virtual
.RI ( provides )
name is a diamond node with an edge to each of its providers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Inspect the package database of an alternate root instead of the live
system.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Write the DOT source to
.I path
instead of standard output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the database cannot be opened or the graph
cannot be exported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-list (1),
.BR tulpar-verify (1)
